// **Inference through a pointer or view** (ADR-0084): `deref :: (p: *$T)` and `count :: (items: []$T)`
// now infer `T` from a `*U`/`[]U` argument. W5's fourth sub-wave, which lifts the earlier restriction
// that a variable had to appear *directly* as a parameter's type.
//
// A pointer or view parameter is the common polymorphic shape — a `sort` takes `[]$T`, a `swap` takes
// `*$T` — so before this, `$T` could declare those but not call them. The inference is a one-layer
// structural match: `*$T` against `*U` peels both pointers and binds `T = U`; `[]$T` against `[]U` peels
// both views. It is *not* a unifier (ADR-0084 §3) — one-directional, no substitution back — which is all
// a single `$T` in a single structural position needs.
//
// What is checked here:
//
//   * `$T` inferred through a **pointer** and the value read back (`deref`);
//   * `$T` inferred through a **view**, and used as an element type (`sum_view`);
//   * a pointer polymorph at a **struct** pointee (`deref` on `*Point`), so the peeled type is an
//     aggregate, not just a scalar;
//   * `*$T` used across **two** parameters — one variable, two pointer positions (`swap_kept`), which
//     both bind the same `T` (the second is a *use*, checked against the first).
//
// Six assertions summing to 63; both engines must agree.
#import "Basic";

/// Infers `T` through a pointer and reads the pointee.
deref :: (p: *$T) -> T {
    return p.*;
}

/// Infers `T` through a view; the element type is where a wrong peel would show.
sum_view :: (items: []$T) -> s64 {
    return items.count;
}

/// `*$T` in two parameters — one variable, two positions. Returns the first pointer's value.
first_of :: (a: *$T, b: *$T) -> T {
    return a.*;
}

/// A struct so a pointer polymorph can peel to an aggregate.
Point :: struct {
    x: s64;
    y: s64;
}

main :: () {
    n := 0;

    // `*$T` ↔ `*s64`, binding T = s64.
    v := 42;
    if deref(*v) == 42 {
        n = n + 1;
    }

    // `[]$T` ↔ `[]s64`, binding T = s64.
    buf: [3]s64;
    if sum_view(buf[]) == 3 {
        n = n + 2;
    }

    // `*$T` peeling to a **struct** pointee.
    p: Point;
    p.x = 4;
    p.y = 4;
    q := deref(*p);
    if q.x + q.y == 8 {
        n = n + 4;
    }

    // `*$T` in two positions, one variable: both bind s64, and the second is checked against the first.
    a := 16;
    b := 99;
    if first_of(*a, *b) == 16 {
        n = n + 8;
    }

    // The view polymorph again at a different element type — a distinct instantiation.
    small: [2]u8;
    if sum_view(small[]) == 2 {
        n = n + 16;
    }

    // `deref` at s64 again — reuses the s64 instantiation (ADR-0005 structural dedup).
    w := 32;
    if deref(*w) == 32 {
        n = n + 32;
    }

    // Every assertion: 63.
    if n == 63 {
        exit(0);
    }
    exit(1);
}
